A||||11||FieroBert||Emissions Foibles||||1||
Z||000000||FieroBert||07-06-2001||07:14 PM||||Failed Az Emissions test today.<P>HC and NOX below requirements but failed on Carbon Monoxide levels - 17.44 vs. requirement of 15.0 grams/mile.<P>Any suggestions on places to start.  Just replace fuel filter, air filter, plugs, and PCV valve.<P>Engine light did come on today just before going for test (first time since owning the car - since Feb), will check the code soon to see if anything there.<P>Thanks for any suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||07-06-2001||09:11 PM||||Carbon Monoxide can only be caused by one thing; she’s running rich. I would start with a new O2 sensor. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBert||07-07-2001||12:39 PM||||OK that's a good start.  I got the old O2 sensor out and happen to notice another pipe going nowhere.<P>This one is about 1" in dia. hose coming from the air cleaner housing going to the firewall.  The hose connects to a pipe runing along the firewall to the middle of the car where it turns up at about a 45 degree angle and has a flared end looking like it should have another hose attached.  Mine doesn't.  Am I missing something else also?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-07-2001||02:00 PM||||That 1" diameter hose should have been  removed from the air cleaner, and the air cleaner fitting capped off as part of one of the recall programs. Otherwise, you're sucking unfiltered air into the engine.<BR>The metal pipe going from the firewall-side valve cover to the rubber intake duct replaces it. You ARE talking about a V-6. right?<P>This should have no effect on the emissions test, though. Still sounds like it's running rich, or has a misfire. Did you change your cap, rotor, and wires?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||07-07-2001||02:06 PM||||Raydars right about that pipe.  But the easiest thing to do is plug this pipe with a rubber cap available in one of those HELP! packs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Santa Cruzer||07-07-2001||02:53 PM||||wHEN MY DAD WENT FOR HIS EMISSION'S TEST HIS TRUCK WAS BURNING OIL BAD,NOW WHAT HE DID WAS KEEP THE OIL A BIT LOW,AND GASED IT UP WITH HIGH TEST AND BABOOM HE PASSED! THIS HAS WORKED FOR MANY PEOPLE IT'S WORTH A TRY..<BR><P>------------------<BR>red candy apple copper burgandy color,tan interior all options,american racing rims,Pioneer Cd Player,pioneer 120w speakers"in factory location",sony ****  amp,and workin' on a girl to go with the package<BR>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroBert||07-07-2001||03:58 PM||||Checked the stored code - 44 - Lean exhaust.  Thought that was ironic since I failed for being too rich.  I am going to take it as a sign the O2 sensor needed changing, which I did this morning.<P>Will also try running some fuel injector cleaner thru the gas tank and see if that helps.<P>Thanks for the advice.  Jim||||reg||1
Z||000007||johnt671||07-07-2001||08:49 PM||||Maybe kind of basic, but it may be worth it to put in a new air filter and try some of that guaranteed to pass emission system cleaner stuff if they still make it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||07-08-2001||02:34 AM||||The O2 is reading lean (low) so it tells the ECM to enrichen the fuel. <P>Assuming the O2 is actually connected, replace it. Exact symptoms of a dead O2.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||deceler8||07-08-2001||09:47 AM||||Drive it about an hour on the interstate before you take the test and make sure it's good and hot. Also avoid any prolonged idling before taking the test.<P>Also be sure to use a gas with oxygenate such as ethanol in it...the extra oxygen in the blend is there to reduce CO levels.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroBert||07-08-2001||11:29 AM||||Thanks for all the tips.  Got the O2 sensor changed and cleaned up a few other things.  By the way, it doesn't take much this time of year to get the temperature up, since it's usually starting out at about 120 degrees before I even get it engine started.||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||07-08-2001||11:46 AM||||Lol! Good point. At least we start in the 70's and then head for the teens by mid-day.<P>I'll bet the new O2 fixes the problem.<P>Terry||||reg||1
